**STEP 1 — DELTA**

- `[CHANGED]` `graphql-api.app.{prod,staging}.cineplex.de` — mutationType parity now proven: 140 vs 140 mutations, list-equality `True`, both responses 4324 B. Prior cycles only compared `queryType` (83==83); the mutation half of the "zero environment partitioning" claim was unverified until now.
- `[CHANGED]` ROOT_CAUSE proven at source level, not inferred: `hunt.yml:212` regex `[^\s"\)\]\}]+` does not exclude the backtick, so any URL quoted in a lead markdown block captures the closing `` ` `` as a literal query byte → HTTP 400. `hunt.yml:225` issues `method='HEAD'` only → the verifier never attempts GET-based GraphQL execution, so every automated `403` is Cloudflare bot-gating a HEAD request, not a backend rejection. This is the mechanism behind the 10-cycle "verification gap" and the 200→400 DoH CNAME regression.
- `NO_NEW_ASSETS` — 132-host inventory, CT diff, and full CNAME sweep all exhausted; no delta since 2026-09-23.
- Live this cycle: 2 requests, both metadata-only GET, `Accept: application/json`, no `Authorization`, ≥2 s apart.

**STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE**

- `[PRIO]` graphql-api.app.{prod,staging}.cineplex.de (schema endpoint),9.25,attack_surface=10; business_value=9; tech_exposure=10; gate_ease=10; cloud_surface=5; freshness=10
