## STEP 1 — DELTA

[NEW] **`/graphql` is a second, independent, unauthenticated GraphQL entry point on both `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de` and `graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de`** — never previously probed with a browser UA. `GET /graphql?query={__typename}` → 200/32 B `{"data":{"__typename":"Query"}}` on both envs, `x-powered-by: Express`, `content-type: application/json`, `server: cloudflare`. Equivalent exposure confirmed, not just reachability: `GET /graphql?query={q:__type(name:"Query"){fields{name}}}` on prod → 200/2316 B, **83 queryType fields** — byte-equal count to the same query on `/`. IDOR structure replicates on the new path: `/graphql?query={userById(id:"0"){id}}` → 200/**744 B** `INVALID_ID` "Invalid Id for type: User id: 0", path `['userById']`, no `Authorization` header; same-cycle control `/graphql?query={currentUser{id}}` → 200/**836 B** `UNAUTHENTICATED`. Both byte-identical to the `/` path.

[NEW] `www.graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de` — inventory host with **no probe record in 20+ cycles** — resolved this cycle: DoH `A` → **Status 3 NXDOMAIN**, authority `amit.ns.cloudflare.com`/`dns.cloudflare.com` SOA; `CNAME` query also Status 3, no answer. Dead entry in the cineplex.de zone, no CNAME, not a takeover candidate.

[CHANGED] Remediation scope for both the introspection finding and the IDOR finding is now **two paths per environment** (`/` and `/graphql`), not one. Any fix, WAF rule, or rate-limit scoped to one path leaves the other open — this is a report-level correction, not a schema curiosity.

[CHANGED] `probe-results.md` 1016 lines, this cycle's 4 entries all `HTTP 403` on `/`-only URLs with the urllib UA. **Zero POST, and zero `/graphql` probes across all cycles** — the automated harness cannot see the second entry point at all, so nothing in the automated log contradicts or supports this finding.

[CHANGED] Method correction to my own prior 27 cycles: the stall was a *depth* problem on `/` (schema exhausted, 0 descriptions, 0 defaults). This cycle's only new fact came from *breadth* on a single unprobed path. Breadth was available the whole time and I did not take it.

