## STEP 1 — DELTA

**[NEW]** `graphql-api.app.{,staging.}cineplex.de` — the GraphQL endpoint is a **wildcard/catch-all mount, not a path list**. 9/9 probed prod paths returned 200 `application/json` with `x-powered-by: Express`, including two no human would configure: `/zzz-no-such-route-9f3a2b` (random token) and `/a/b/c/graphql` (3-segment nonsense). On the *invented* path: introspection 200/2316 B = **83 queryType fields** (byte-equal to `/` and `/graphql`), `userById(id:"0")` → 200/**744 B** `INVALID_ID` + `decodePublicId` stacktrace, `currentUser` → 200/**836 B** `UNAUTHENTICATED`. Both byte-identical to `/`. Staging mirrors it (200/32 B on the same invented path).
**[NEW]** `x-amz-apigw-id: EVIA2E8kFiAEChA=` + `cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC` on the arbitrary path → origin execution (API Gateway behind Express), not edge caching. A wildcard mount is the only reading consistent with a random-token path answering.
**[CHANGED]** **CORRECTION, retracting my own last-cycle claim** that "remediation scope is two paths per environment (`/` and `/graphql`)". That was a 2-element sample asserted as a complete set — the same evidence-depth error I have now made three times, in a fourth form. Correct statement: the path space is unbounded, so **path-scoped remediation (WAF rule, path allow/deny-list, "hide the endpoint") is not a viable mitigation.** The fix belongs in the resolver/authorization layer or at host level.
**[CHANGED]** `/graphiql`, `/voyager`, `/playground` → all 200 **JSON**, no IDE bundle. That branch of last cycle's NEXT is closed. `Accept: text/html` on any path → Apollo landing-page shell (1750 B, static CDN React, `isProd:false`) — service fingerprinting, descriptive class, not a separate finding.
**[CHANGED]** `web-dev.cineplex.de` dangle re-verified **18th consecutive cycle** this cycle (DoH CNAME Status 0 TTL 300 → `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458…`; A-follow Status 3 NXDOMAIN, authority `ns1-35.azure-dns.com` SOA). Freshness restored; evidence is submission-fresh.

