## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION

**[NEXT]** PROBE: test credentialed CORS on the wildcard GraphQL mount, an axis unexamined in 27+ cycles. Two read-only GETs with an `Origin` header, ≥2 s apart, no `Authorization`, on `https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/zzz-no-such-route-9f3a2b`:
`curl -s -D - -o /dev/null -H 'Origin: https://attacker.example' -H 'Accept: application/json' -G --data-urlencode 'query={__typename}' 'https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/zzz-no-such-route-9f3a2b'`
then the same with `-H 'Cookie: probe=1'` to read `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` / `Access-Control-Allow-Headers` on the response.
**Kill condition:** if `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` is absent, or is a bare `*`, or is echoed **without** `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`, reject immediately — that is the CORS-without-credentials class already rejected for `analytics.systems.cineplex.de`, and I will not re-litigate it here. Escalate only on reflected origin **plus** `Allow-Credentials: true`, which on an unbounded-path mount with a JWT/refresh-token session would be a genuine ATO-class vector. Do not send a real token or cookie value.

