**H2 — `graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de`: unauthenticated confirmation-code request is environment-gated, and the failing request discloses an internal route and tenant id, confidence 85.** Design is a code oracle: the field returns `String`, and the caller-chosen `type` routes the lookup. Prod enforces `FORBIDDEN "only available in testing environments"`; staging enforces nothing and calls LOGIN, echoing `extensions.status`, `extensions.url` and `mandatorId=746241be-…` to an unauthenticated caller. What I did **not** establish: any returned code. The 405 means the downstream call was rejected on method, so the previous "Reset code disclosed" inference remains unsupported. Two separable claims: disclosure = confirmed, unauthenticated, submittable; code extraction = open, needs a consented staging account.

