## Objective
- Continue Cineplex bug-hunt analysis in `POC` phase for target `api`, prioritizing report-ready GraphQL/auth/business-logic flaws.
- Produce only the required structured analyst blocks while keeping live testing passive-first, read-only, and PII-safe.

## Important Details
- Scope: Cineplex-owned infrastructure only. Explicitly reject TLS best practices, username enumeration, descriptive-only errors/headers, known-vulnerable libraries without exploit, DoS/lockout, logout CSRF, and similar listed exclusions.
- Live probes: ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; no auth-bypass, mutation, login, DNS modification, claim attempt, real credential, or customer-data exposure.
- Primary hosts: `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de` and `graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de`.
- GraphQL reaches origin through `/`, `/graphql`, `/v1/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, and arbitrary catch-all paths. Balanced URL-encoded GET plus browser UA returns `200`; automated urllib often gets Cloudflare `403`.
- `probe-results.md` is unreliable: trailing-backtick URLs cause `400`, urllib UA triggers the bot gate, and the log has zero POST probes. Use own manual captures.
- Corrections superseding historical KB claims:
  - “No injection vectors” was name-only and false; eight URL/credential-shaped arguments exist. Introspection severity was re-scored `5.3 → 7.5`.
  - “10 staging-only mutations” was caused by mismatched `includeDeprecated`; both environments expose identical totals.
  - A type was not considered read until its field list was inspected.
- `reports/analyst-nemotron3.log` is peer output and must not be adopted as evidence.
- Current stated risk: `2/100`; no valid customer identifiers or PII requested.

## Work State
### Completed
- Exhausted the 132-host inventory, CT diff, and CNAME sweep; no new non-inventory assets.
- Confirmed unauthenticated introspection on both GraphQL environments:
  - 83 active + 5 deprecated queries; 140 active + 10 deprecated mutations.
  - 385 types, including 44 `INPUT_OBJECT` types.
  - Argument/type/input-object evidence was captured through balanced GET; `x-powered-by: Express` and `x-amz-apigw-id` confirm origin execution.
- Confirmed dual independent entry points `/` and `/graphql`; `/graphql` returns `200`/32 B `__typename` on both environments and carries the same schema/resolvers.
- Confirmed catch-all GraphQL mounting on arbitrary paths; fixes cannot be scoped to a route.
- Structurally confirmed pre-auth ID decoding across `userById`, `invoice`, `order`, and `ticket`:
  - Synthetic `id:"0"` reaches `decodePublicId` and returns `200`/`INVALID_ID`.
  - `currentUser` and six sibling controls return `UNAUTHENTICATED`/`FORBIDDEN`.
  - All tested synthetic/well-formed fake IDs return the same typed error; no enumeration oracle found.
- Expanded static blast radius:
  - `User` has 51 fields, including identity, `onlineTicketingToken`, `inviteCode`, linked accounts, privileges, orders, invoices, and tickets.
  - `order → user` and `ticket → order → user` reach `User` without `userById`.
  - `userByQr` maps a physical QR artifact to a digital identity.
- Identified name-for-name mass-assignment mirrors, without execution:
  - `CinemaOperatingCompanyData.accessRight*` versus `UserPrivileges.accessRight*`.
  - `updateUser(adminCinemaOperatingCompanyIds)` versus computed cinema-admin fields.
  - `increaseUserTestingStatus(testingStatus)` versus `User.testingStatus`.
- Closed the proposed unauthenticated SSRF: `getOnlineTicketingBooking` is root-gated before input handling on prod and staging.
- Reconfirmed `web-dev.cineplex.de` dangling CNAME for 18 cycles:
  - `web-dev.cineplex.de CNAME web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io`
  - Target A lookup returns NXDOMAIN with Azure SOA.
  - It is the sole CNAME in the swept dev/systems sets.
- Dev origin behavior remains backend/network-gated: SPAs return `200`, `/gateway/*` returns `503 "Wartungsarbeiten"`, with intermittent TCP `000`.

### Active
- Ranked candidate `[99]`: `GraphQL Dual Entry Point + Full Type/Argument Surface Exposure on Production` in `art/lead_nemotron3.txt`.
- IDOR candidate at confidence `84`: structural pre-auth decode and broad `User` blast radius are proven; ownership impact remains unverified.
- AUTH candidate at confidence `71`: `login(privileged:Boolean)` and `refreshLogin(refreshToken:String!, privileged:Boolean)` on staging; no credentialed test performed.
- MISCONFIG candidate at confidence `93`: dangling `web-dev.cineplex.de` CNAME; provider-side claimability remains outstanding.
- `testing_getConfirmationCode` reaches staging’s internal LOGIN route while prod returns `FORBIDDEN`, but no confirmation code was extracted. Later KB treatment rejects it standalone unless code minting is demonstrated.
- Schema-only mutation candidates remain unexecuted, including `startWebBooking`, `logUserScreeningInterests`, `sendNotifications`, `deleteCineplexUser`, `updateUser`, `storeSDKLogin`, and `storeConsent`.

### Blocked
- IDOR proof needs one consented account’s own `publicId`; cross-tenant proof then needs a second consented account. Query `__typename` only—never customer fields.
- `privileged` behavior needs one consented low-privilege staging account and identical login/refresh comparisons.
- Confirmation-code impact needs a consented address and extraction; do not use real customer data.
- Dangling-CNAME takeover needs Azure confirmation that `gentleglacier-dfef6458` is deprovisioned and claimable.
- `probe-results.md` cannot validate GraphQL conclusions because it contains zero POST and only root/malformed GET probes.
- Triage `run-2026-09-26-01:56.md` failed with `UnknownError` / `ref err_b491aaa2`; reposcan remains unconfigured with `TARGET_ORG not configured`.

## Next Move
1. Probe only synthetic IDs on `https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/v1/graphql` using balanced `curl -G --data-urlencode`, browser UA, `Accept: application/json`, and ≥2-second spacing: `order(id:"1")`, `ticket(id:"1")`, `invoice(id:"1")`, plus `order(id:"0")` control; record status, byte length, and `extensions.code`. Stop on any resolution or different error shape and do not widen the ID space.
2. If all return `INVALID_ID`, sweep unswept required-argument Query fields one at a time on `https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/api/graphql` using obvious dummy values and `{__typename}` only, prioritizing `voucherInstanceByQR`, `voucherInstancesByOrderNumber`, `checkVoucherCode`, `userByQr`, `beaconById`, `notification`, `targetGroup`, `getImdbIds`, and `reverseGeocode`; skip `testing_forceDeleteUser` and stop on resolution or `extensions.url`.

