## MY STATE
Phase: POC · Target: api · Risk: 2/100 · Mode: passive-first, GET only, ≤1 rps

## OBJECTIVE
Close the pre-auth resolver inventory on `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de`, determine whether the ID-decode-before-auth pattern is systemic, and test the two unprobed unauthenticated URL/geocode surfaces for SSRF. Record only what my own manual balanced-GET captures prove.

## IMPORTANT DETAILS
- **My own record was wrong on the key number.** It said 4 pre-auth ID decoders. This cycle proves **18 non-gated, id-bearing, unauthenticated resolvers**. I also found the `atob()` id decoder plus an unauthenticated unhandled exception, and closed SSRF on two fields.
- Automated log is still broken: `probe-results.md` is now **1052 lines, zero POST**, every GraphQL line `403` (urllib UA), DoH lines `400` (trailing backtick). All evidence below is from my own `curl --http2` + browser UA + `-G --data-urlencode` captures.
- `externalUrl(appDeepLink:"javascript:alert(1)")` → `403` at the **WAF**, not the app. Descriptive-error material; I am not reporting it.
- Latency was my decisive control: `appDeepLink` returned `0.2185s / 0.2257s / 0.2204s` for three different hosts, including a closed loopback port. Identical timing means **no server-side fetch**, so `appDeepLink` is a pure string classifier.
- **Correction to my own introspection:** my earlier required-arg list came from a shallow 2-level `ofType` read, so LIST args and renamed args were wrong — `voucherCatalog` takes `cinemaId` (not `id`), `screeningAuditorium` takes `screeningId`, `bonusPrograms`/`movies` take `ids`, `screenedMovies`/`campaignsByCinemas`/`incomingForeignMovieIdentifiers`/`allCinemaFilmSeries` take `cinemaIds`. Re-read at 88 Query fields this cycle.
- The Google attribution is verbatim provider text, not inference: `"Invalid request. Invalid 'latlng' parameter."` raised as `UserInputError` at `/var/task/graphql.js:15383`.
- Third distinct error code observed: `PosDevicesOnly` ("Only POS Devices are allowed to query this endpoint") on `voucherInstanceByQR`, firing **before** the qrCode argument is even examined.

## COMPLETED
- **Control:** brand-new never-before-probed path `/zz/q9/x1` → `200`, 32B, resolved. Catch-all GraphQL mounting confirmed on a path absent from all prior captures.
- **Closed SSRF on `appDeepLink(externalUrl:)`.** `https://www.cineplex.com/`, `https://cineplex.com/`, and `http://127.0.0.1:1/` all returned `BAD_USER_INPUT / UNKNOWN_HOST` at `~0.22s`. Transform, not fetch. No SSRF.
- **Characterized `externalUrl(appDeepLink:)` and contained it.** It is an allowlisted router, not a generic dispatcher: `cineplex://movie/1` → `INVALID_ID "Invalid Id for type: Movie id: 1"`, so it reaches the pre-auth Movie decoder. But `user`, `order`, `invoice`, `ticket`, `cinema` → `UNKNOWN_PATH`; `//example.com/x`, `/movies`, `data:text/html,x` → `UNKNOWN_SCHEME`. The PII types are **not** routable through the deep link.
- **New unauthenticated server-side third-party call: `reverseGeocode(latitude, longitude)`** → `ReverseGeocodeResult{route,postalCode,locality,country}`. Berlin → `postalCode:10178, locality:Berlin, country:Germany`. Provider is **Google Maps Geocoding API** (verbatim error text). Arguments are forwarded to Google **before range validation** — `latitude:1000, longitude:1000` was forwarded and returned Google's own `latlng` complaint. Coordinates are GraphQL `Float`, so ±90 is enforced at the schema layer: **no host control, no parameter injection, no SSRF.** No API key appeared in any error path. Staging parity confirmed identical (`country: "Germany"`, 50B).
- **Proved the ID scheme is base64 and found an unauthenticated unhandled exception.** `contentSectionList(id:"0")` and `movieList(id:"0")` both returned `200` with `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR / "Invalid character: the string to be decoded is not correctly encoded."` — the WHATWG `atob` `InvalidCharacterError`, with a stacktrace leaking `/var/task/graphql.js`. Trigger is length-based: `"AA"` and `"AAAA"` return `INVALID_ID` normally; only `len % 4 != 0` throws.
- **Proved the crash does not reach the sensitive decoders.** `userById`, `order`, `ticket`, `invoice` with `id:"A"` (len%4≠0) and with `id:"!!!!"` (non-base64 chars) all returned `INVALID_ID`, no exception, 739–750B. The PII decoders use a different, tolerant decoder. Crash class is confined to two content resolvers.
- **Closed the enumeration question on the PII id space.** `userById(id:"AAAA")` and `order(id:"AAAA")` — well-formed synthetic base64 — still return `INVALID_ID`, so the base64 disclosure from `atob` does not transfer to `User`/`Order`. The PII id space is not cheaply enumerable. Prior conclusion holds, now for a proven reason.
- **Swept all 47 required-argument Query fields** (single `__typename`, obviously-synthetic dummies, ≥2s spacing, `testing_forceDeleteUser` deliberately not invoked).

Pre-auth, **no auth gate, reaches entity logic** (18):

| Resolver | Observed at synthetic id |
|---|---|
| `userById` / `order` / `ticket` / `invoice` | `INVALID_ID` for User / Order / Ticket / Invoice |
| `movie` | `ENTITY_NOT_FOUND "No movie with this id exists: N"` |
| `cinema` | `null`, **error suppressed** |
| `screening` / `company` / `newsItem` / `notification` | `INVALID_ID` |
| `bonusProgram` | `InvalidBonusProgramId` (non-camelCase code) |
| `similarMovies(movieId:)` | `INVALID_ID` for Movie |
| `soonInCinemaItems` / `voucherCatalog` / `screenedMovies` | `INVALID_ID` for Cinema |
| `contentSectionList` / `movieList` | `atob` crash, then `INVALID_ID` |
| `reverseGeocode` | resolved, third-party call |
| `voucherInstancesByOrderNumber` | `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` |

Correctly gated: `cinemaCluster`, `targetGroup` (`UNAUTHENTICATED`); `checkVoucherCode` (`UNAUTHENTICATED`); `userByQr` (`FORBIDDEN / DEVICE_UNAUTHORIZED`); `voucherInstanceByQR` (`PosDevicesOnly`); `campaignsByCinemas`, `beaconById` (`FORBIDDEN / only available for admin users`); `estimateCampaignSize`, `screeningAuditorium`; `getImdbIds` (`BAD_API_KEY` — internal upstream credential validation surfaced to an anonymous caller); `cinfinityCinemaStats`, `payoutInfo`.
- **Best evidence of inconsistency, same cycle:** `cinemaCluster(id:)` is gated but `cinema(id:)` is open; `targetGroup` is gated but `notification(id:)` is open; `campaignsByCinemas` is admin-gated but `screenedMovies` is open; `soonInCinemaItems(cinemaId:)` rejects id `0` with `INVALID_ID` while `cinema(id:)` returns bare `null` for the identical id.
- Two `IS NOT` noise items closed: `searchMovie(title:"0")` returns 16 `Movie` objects and `searchCastOrCrewMember(fullName:"0")` returns 6 `CastOrCrewMember` — input is ignored, public marketing content, not a finding.
- Dangle reconfirmed, now **cycle 19**: CNAME intact, `A` → `Status: 3` (NXDOMAIN), authority `switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io` SOA, `getent` no A record.
- Staging full parity on every new surface (`reverseGeocode` resolved, `cinema` 25B null, `movie` `ENTITY_NOT_FOUND`, `userById` 744B `INVALID_ID`).

## ACTIVE
- **IDOR candidate, confidence 84 → 88.** The structural argument is now much stronger and no longer depends on cherry-picked resolvers: 18 unauthenticated resolvers reach entity logic before any gate, the gate is demonstrably hand-applied and inconsistent on identical types, and the PII `User` object carries 51 fields including `onlineTicketingToken`, `inviteCode`, and `testingStatus`. Impact still unproven.
- **New candidate, low-to-moderate: unauthenticated server-side third-party API proxy (`reverseGeocode`).** Anonymous callers drive outbound requests against a customer-billed Google Maps key, with arguments forwarded before validation. Honest limit: I have not shown a billing or availability impact, the ±90 Float ceiling blocks SSRF, and no credential leaked. Realistic ceiling is a low-severity inventory/misconfiguration note.
- **`movie(id:)` is a clean pre-auth existence oracle, informational only.** `ENTITY_NOT_FOUND` means the id *format was accepted* and the lookup missed, versus `INVALID_ID` which means format rejection. `movie(id:"1")` and `id:"0"` both miss. Movie titles are public, so this is documentation of the oracle mechanism, not a vulnerability.
- Dangle, confidence 93, unchanged and still provider-blocked.
- `AUTH` (`login`/`refreshLogin` `privileged:Boolean`), confidence 71, unchanged, still uncredentialed.

## BLOCKED
- IDOR impact needs **one consented account's own `publicId`**, queried as `{__typename}` only. Cross-tenant needs a second consented account. Without it the PII-reach claim stays structural.
- The PII id space is now provably not brute-forceable, which means I will **not** search it. Enumeration is out of bounds and unnecessary.
- `reverseGeocode` needs no block, but I will not escalate to quota/consumption testing — that is rate-limit and resource-exhaustion territory, explicitly excluded.
- `appDeepLink`/`externalUrl` oracle value is capped at disclosure, and descriptive-error material is excluded, so I will not build a report around `UNKNOWN_HOST`/`UNKNOWN_SCHEME`.
- Dangle claimability still needs Azure confirmation that `gentleglacier-dfef6458` is deprovisioned.
- Reposcan still unconfigured (`TARGET_ORG not configured`); `run-2026-09-26-01:56.md` still `UnknownError` / `ref err_b491aaa2`.

