1. Single new dimension, safe: test whether the `atob` crash class reaches the **Mutation** surface's id-bearing arguments, since mutations are where an unauthenticated pre-auth decode would matter most. Use one obviously-synthetic malformed id per field, `{__typename}` only, no execution, on `https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/api/graphql`. Expect `UNAUTHENTICATED` for all of them; any field that reaches decode logic pre-auth is a genuine escalation. Skip `testing_forceDeleteUser` and every state-changing field.
2. If step 1 is uniformly gated as expected, the pre-auth IDOR question is exhausted for unauthenticated testing. Pivot to consolidating the report bundle around the two defensible items — the 18-resolver pre-auth IDOR (impact pending one consented id) and the dangling CNAME — and record `reverseGeocode` as a low-severity appendix note rather than a headline.

