**STEP 1 — DELTA**

- [NEW] **Inconsistent authorization proven by controlled comparison.** Same host, same cycle, no `Authorization`, same valid public id `Q2luZW1hOjIzOQ==` (base64 `Cinema:239` = Capitol Aachen): `cinema(id:)` → 200/44B **populated**, `contentSectionListByNameAndCinemas(cinemaIds:)` → 200/665B **`UNAUTHENTICATED`** at `selectedCinemaIdsDb` :40870. Only the resolver name differs.
- [NEW] `movie(id:"TW92aWU6Mjg3MTk=")` → 200/42B **populated**, no check — a *second* ungated resolver on a different decoder contract.
- [NEW] Public id namespaces are enumerable unauthenticated: `cinemas{id name}` → 92 records (2231B), `allMovies{id title}` → 12933 records (798141B). This is what made the falsification possible with zero PII.
- [NEW] 15th family member, first **list-shaped** argument: `cinemaIds:[ID]!` decoded inside `Array.map` :15095:127; enum `ContentSectionListName` = {CURATED, RECOMMENDED}; staging byte-identical at 766B.
- [NEW] Impact measured, not assumed: `Movie` = 26 fields of public catalogue; `MovieStatistics` = only `numWatchlistings` + `numInteractions`, no revenue; 3 currentUser-scoped fields correctly per-session.
- [NEW] Ungated read reproduces on `/graphql` (200/44B) → a single-path fix is incomplete. Staging returns a **third** behaviour, `{"data":{"cinema":null}}` (200/25B).
- [CHANGED] `INVALID_ID` discriminator **falsified**; family enumeration complete at 20 fields / 15 pre-auth / 6 gates.
- [CHANGED] dangle re-verified 20th cycle (CNAME Status 0, TTL 300). Harness defect shown same-cycle: pipeline logged 403 for the exact enum URL I fetched at 200.

