Both CORS leads are now dead, with positive evidence. `profil.cineplex.de` sets a cookie but emits **no `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` at all** — the browser will not expose the response to any cross-origin page, and the `JSESSIONID` has no `SameSite` attribute (defaults to `Lax` in modern browsers, so it isn't attached to cross-site XHR anyway). And the GraphQL host, which does reflect `null` + `ACAC: true`, sets no cookie whatsoever, and the schema's `login` returns `jwt`/`refreshToken`/`csrf` in the response body (bearer-token auth, no ambient cookie) while custom-header preflight is `403`.

