[PARKED] "Mutations executable via GET on `/`." The single highest-value unverified claim in this whole bundle. GraphQL-over-GET is spec-legal and `/` serves full execution over GET, so the 140 mutations may well be reachable from a plain link, an `<img>` tag, a crawler prefetch, or a shared cache — which would make them CSRF-able and cache-poisonable with no CORS involvement at all. I cannot test it without sending a mutation document, so I am leaving it unclaimed and naming it. If a tester with an account confirms it, that outranks everything in this block.
[PARKED] `Order.pickupCode:Int` and `User.onlineTicketingToken` exposure: schema shape on resolvers whose authorization I have not measured. Filing asserts impact I cannot support — the error class I retracted twice on 09-26.
[PARKED] HTTP 500 on disallowed `Origin`: real, pre-routing, now well-characterized. Network DoS and descriptive errors are both explicit exclusions. Mechanism proof only.

[FINAL] 1. Credentialed cross-origin POST on the production GraphQL API — 90 — `null`, `http://localhost:3000` and `https://app.staging.cineplex.de` all preflight-approved with `ACAC: true`, POST + `authorization` allowed, 6/6, both envs; Tier 1 proven, Tier 2 AUTH_HELPED
[FINAL] 2. Same grant on staging, landing on an unauthenticated mutation — 78 — `testing_getConfirmationCode` has no environment guard
[FINAL] 3. GET-only mirrors misread as equivalent transports — 70 — `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql` cannot receive POST; the 97% parity claim was a method-blind artifact
[FINAL] 4. (carried) Unauthenticated full-schema introspection, 83 queries + 140 mutations, 385 types, byte-identical across all four GET routes — 95 — CVSS 7.5
[FINAL] 5. (carried) Dangling CNAME web-dev.cineplex.de → azurecontainerapps.io, 17+ cycles NXDOMAIN — 96 — PASSIVE

[NEXT] PROBE: the Tier 1 / Tier 2 boundary cannot be crossed by any unauthenticated request, so I am done probing. One account-gated step remains and it is a human action, not a probe: with a consented test account, open a page served with `Content-Security-Policy: sandbox` and issue `fetch("https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/", {method:"POST", credentials:"include", headers:{"content-type":"application/json"}, body:'{"query":"{currentUser{id}}"}'})`. If the response body comes back non-null from that opaque origin, Tier 2 is proven and the finding is High. If it returns `UNAUTHENTICATED` exactly as my cookie-injection probe did, the honest ceiling is Tier 1 and the report says Medium-as-origin-trust with the credential dependency named. No mutation in either branch.

[LEARN] ACCEPTED cors_preflight_credentialed_post @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: `OPTIONS /` returns 204 with `ACAO: <attacker origin>`, `ACAC: true`, `ACAM` including POST, `ACAH: content-type,authorization` for `null`, `http://localhost:3000` and `https://app.staging.cineplex.de`, on both environments — 6/6. This is the missing half of last cycle's finding: I had proven the ACAO/ACAC pair on *responses*, which proves reflection but not that a browser would let a third-party page issue the write. The preflight is what proves the write is permitted. Confidence 75 → 90, and the finding moved from "policy defect" to "unauthenticated call primitive".
[LEARN] ACCEPTED getonly_graphql_mirrors @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de{/,/graphql,/api/graphql,/gql}: POST and OPTIONS to `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql` return API-GW 403 `MissingAuthenticationTokenException` with no `x-powered-by: Express` and no `x-amz-trace-id`, while `POST /` returns 200. Three of the four routes are GET-only read mirrors. Directly contradicts my own 97% "4 equivalent surfaces" claim from 2026-09-28.
[LEARN] REJECTED my own 2026-09-28 `4 equivalent unauthenticated full-schema GraphQL surfaces` @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: I measured equivalence in exactly one dimension — the GET response body — and generalised it to the transport. Identical bytes on GET says nothing about what the route accepts on POST, and the answer differs. Method-vary every equivalence claim I make about an endpoint. Two of my three headline claims this cycle rested on a single method, and one of them was wrong.
[LEARN] REJECTED my own 2026-09-26 interpretation of "zero POST captures" in `probe-results.md`: those POSTs returned 403, not absence. I read a gateway rejection as a missing capability. The literal-trailing-backtick and urllib-UA defects in that harness are real, but "the tool never saw a successful POST" was never evidence that no successful POST exists — I just proved one.

[RISK] cineplex: 68 (up 8). Driven by one thing measured six times this cycle: a production API that preflight-approves credentialed cross-origin POST for an opaque `null` origin, a developer loopback origin, and a staging origin, on the only route that can actually receive a mutation, in the environment pair that also hosts an unguarded testing resolver. Not higher, because the credential-dependent tier is still unproven and I refused to probe it with a mutation. The GET-only-mirror correction *lowered* the introspection finding's score and that is the honest trade — a smaller surface with a real write primitive on it is a worse posture than a large surface you cannot write to.
