## Objective
- Continue authorized Cineplex bug-bounty analysis in `POC`/`api` and output only the requested eight structured analysis blocks with up to three non-out-of-scope hypotheses.

## Important Details
- Scope only Cineplex-controlled assets in `scope.yml` and `inventory/cineplex.md`.
- Separate confirmed facts from hypotheses; do not invent impact.
- Live verification must be passive-first, ≤1 rps, and limited to read-only GET/HEAD/OPTIONS; no auth bypass, destructive requests, or customer-data access.
- Scanner output requires manual validation; hash any secret with SHA-256.
- Explicitly reject username enumeration, TLS best-practice issues, logout CSRF, descriptive errors, generic known-vulnerable libraries, standalone OPTIONS/TRACE, DoS/lockout, and other listed exclusions.
- Step 4 must drop confidence `<40`, rejected-class, or unverifiable hypotheses.
- Emit exactly one `[NEXT]` action.
- Canonical corrections supersede repeated historical lines: “no injection vectors/CVSS 5.3” was based on a name-only read; IDOR authorization omission was falsified; route equivalence cannot be inferred from GET alone.
- Current canonical live leads are CORS, mass assignment, and dangling CNAME; repeated history is not independent re-verification.

## Work State
### Completed
- Exhausted the 132-host baseline, CT diff, and CNAME sweep; latest inventory delta is empty.
- Added `## CANONICAL STATUS (2026-09-30)` to `knowledge/index.md`, partitioned into LIVE / DEAD / SURVIVING / METHOD RULES, and marked 11 resurrected claims `[SUPERSEDED]`.
- Verified unauthenticated GraphQL introspection on `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de` and `graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de`: 88 total queries (`83` active + `5` deprecated) and 150 total mutations (`140` active + `10` deprecated), with staging parity.
- Clarified route topology: `/` and `/graphql` are unauthenticated GraphQL entry points; `/api/graphql` and `/gql` are GET-only read mirrors whose POST/OPTIONS reach API Gateway `403 MissingAuthenticationTokenException`.
- Confirmed production CORS policy: `null`, `http://localhost:3000`, and `https://app.staging.cineplex.de` are reflected with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`; preflight on `/` permits `GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE,OPTIONS` and `content-type,authorization`.
- Falsified IDOR authorization omission: `INVALID_ID` versus `UNAUTHENTICATED` only proves decoder position; valid public cinema IDs reached an auth check. Only pre-auth decoder reach survives.
- Rejected `testing_getConfirmationCode` as standalone, `getOnlineTicketingBooking` SSRF, relay metrics/saturation, `api.cineplex.de` bypass, Nextcloud version disclosure, booking-dev origin bypass, and TLS-dead hosts.
- Confirmed `web-dev.cineplex.de` CNAME `Status 0` to `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io`; target follow-up is `Status 3 NXDOMAIN` with Azure SOA.
- Verified `scripts/sync-issues.py` only publishes `[HYP]` blocks from `leads/lead-*.md`; falsified IDOR text is `[LEARN]` and cannot leak.

### Active
- CORS hypothesis, confidence `95`: browser credential exploitation remains `AUTH_HELPED`; dummy cookies did not establish an accepted session.
- Mass-assignment hypothesis, confidence `85`: `CinemaOperatingCompanyData.accessRightDashboard/FilmStatistics/BonusProgram/Campaigning` exactly mirrors derived `UserPrivileges`; mutation gates remain unexecuted.
- Dangling-CNAME hypothesis, confidence `96`: takeover precondition is confirmed, but Azure provider claimability is not.
- Latest `16:26` cycle made no new live request; `probe-results.md` ends at `2026-09-30 10:06:19`.

### Blocked
- CORS impact needs a consented valid session and browser-side credentialed request; do not infer it from dummy cookies.
- Mass assignment needs a consented test account and program-approved execution proving caller-supplied flags reach `UserPrivileges`.
- CNAME takeover needs provider-side claimability attestation; do not register Azure resources without authorization.
- Pipeline GraphQL URLs contain trailing backticks and urllib hits the bot gate, producing false `400/403`; manual balanced `curl -G --data-urlencode` with browser UA returns `200`.
- Pipeline DoH handling is not durable; `Accept: application/dns-json` is load-bearing.
- `reposcan` remains unconfigured with `TARGET_ORG not configured`.

