## Objective
- Continue authorized Cineplex bug-bounty analysis in `POC`/`api` and output only the requested eight structured analysis blocks with up to three non-out-of-scope hypotheses.

## Important Details
- Scope only Cineplex-controlled assets in `scope.yml` and `inventory/cineplex.md`.
- Separate confirmed facts from hypotheses; do not invent impact.
- Live verification must be passive-first, ≤1 rps, and limited to read-only GET/HEAD/OPTIONS; no auth bypass, destructive requests, or customer-data access.
- Scanner output requires manual validation; hash any secret with SHA-256.
- Explicitly reject username enumeration, TLS best-practice issues, logout CSRF, descriptive errors, generic known-vulnerable libraries, standalone OPTIONS/TRACE, DoS/lockout, and other listed exclusions.
- Step 4 must drop confidence `<40`, rejected-class, or unverifiable hypotheses.
- Emit exactly one `[NEXT]` action.
- Canonical corrections supersede repeated historical lines: “no injection vectors/CVSS 5.3” was based on a name-only read; IDOR authorization omission was falsified; route equivalence cannot be inferred from GET alone.
- Current canonical live leads are CORS, mass assignment, and dangling CNAME; repeated history is not independent re-verification.

