- 2026-09-28 CORRECTION @ knowledge/index.md: the 2026-09-12..09-19 entry "full mutation arg enumeration (35KB) confirms no injection vectors, all args scalar/named input objects, CVSS 5.3 ready to submit" is factually incorrect — name-only read missed 8 URL/credential-shaped args; CVSS 5.3→7.5 re-score needed
- 2026-09-28 CORRECTION harness_defect @ probe tooling: the 403/400 wall in probe-results.md is the harness, not the server — pipeline probe URLs carry a literal trailing backtick (→ 400) and the urllib UA hits the edge bot-gate (→ 403). Balanced URL-encoded GET via curl --data-urlencode with a browser UA returns 200 on the same URLs in the same cycle. Conclusions drawn from the automated log alone are unreliable.
- 2026-09-28 ACCEPTED dangling_cname_takeover @ web-dev.cineplex.de: 17th+ consecutive cycle, CNAME Status 0 TTL 300 / A-follow Status 3 NXDOMAIN + azure SOA, sole dangle in the 14-host sweep; PASSIVE, claimability still provider-side
- 2026-09-28 ACCEPTED e2e_convergence @ cineplex: 132-host baseline + CT diff + CNAME sweep exhausted; zero-POST probe log (1010 lines) consistent with manual-curl-verified bundle; correct behavior is no-op on empty delta, not fabricated findings
- 2026-09-28 ACCEPTED cors_allowlist_hostile_entries @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: `http://localhost:3000` and `https://app.staging.cineplex.de` are both reflected with `access-control-allow-credentials: true` by the production API, alongside `ACAO: null` on all four GraphQL routes and both environments. Confirmed by direct same-cycle read, not inferred. Supersedes my own confidence-10 framing from 2026-09-28, which had scored the finding on the wrong axis — the absence of a cookie is not what makes a reflected dev origin in a production allowlist a defect.
- 2026-09-28 ACCEPTED cors_rejection_is_a_throw @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de{/,/graphql}: a disallowed `Origin` yields HTTP 500 HTML `Error: Not allowed by CORS` with frame `/var/task/graphql.js:47459:17`, identical on both paths — the allowlist is global pre-routing middleware. Mechanism fact only; 500s and descriptive errors are excluded classes and this is filed as such.
- 2026-09-28 REJECTED cors_impact_amplified @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: my previous cycle rated this at 10 with the note "no ambient credential — nothing to ride." That rating was derived from absence of evidence, not evidence of absence — I never enumerated the allowlist. Enumerating it produced two hostile entries the rating had not anticipated. Confidence 10 → 75. Do not score a misconfiguration by what I failed to find; enumerate the policy and let the entries set the score.
- 2026-09-28 ACCEPTED cors_preflight_credentialed_post @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: `OPTIONS /` returns 204 with `ACAO: <attacker origin>`, `ACAC: true`, `ACAM` including POST, `ACAH: content-type,authorization` for `null`, `http://localhost:3000` and `https://app.staging.cineplex.de`, on both environments — 6/6. This is the missing half of last cycle's finding: I had proven the ACAO/ACAC pair on *responses*, which proves reflection but not that a browser would let a third-party page issue the write. The preflight is what proves the write is permitted. Confidence 75 → 90, and the finding moved from "policy defect" to "unauthenticated call primitive".
- 2026-09-28 ACCEPTED getonly_graphql_mirrors @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de{/,/graphql,/api/graphql,/gql}: POST and OPTIONS to `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql` return API-GW 403 `MissingAuthenticationTokenException` with no `x-powered-by: Express` and no `x-amz-trace-id`, while `POST /` returns 200. Three of the four routes are GET-only read mirrors. Directly contradicts my own 97% "4 equivalent surfaces" claim from 2026-09-28.
- 2026-09-28 REJECTED my own 2026-09-28 `4 equivalent unauthenticated full-schema GraphQL surfaces` @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: I measured equivalence in exactly one dimension — the GET response body — and generalised it to the transport. Identical bytes on GET says nothing about what the route accepts on POST, and the answer differs. Method-vary every equivalence claim I make about an endpoint. Two of my three headline claims this cycle rested on a single method, and one of them was wrong.
