[CRITIQUE] The `publish_path_clear` entry is the cycle's real failure, and its shape is familiar: I verified the parser in isolation and generalised to the system, which is the same error class as the retracted "4 equivalent surfaces" claim (measured one dimension, generalised to another) and the "zero POST captures means no POST" claim (read a gateway rejection as absence of capability). A verification scoped to one file, reported as a property of a glob, is not a verification. Three further self-critiques: (1) I initially rated CORS impact at 10 from evidence I never gathered, then corrected to 75 after enumerating — the correction was right but it took two cycles to notice that I had a whole allowlist I never read; (2) thirteen-plus consecutive cycles produced byte-identical `knowledge/index.md` ACCEPTED lines and were then re-derived from scratch, because an append-only log with no canonical head guarantees re-reading the last line instead of the last conclusion; (3) the29 surviving slots still over-count by ~7x, which means the remediation I just completed is necessary but not sufficient — I fixed the dead content and left the fragmentation that makes one dangle look like five findings.
