Done. The publish set is now clean and verified.

**Correction to the prior summary:** its "completed" state was false. The tree was clean at commit `eacf870` — the 703 retags were never persisted. Real measured prior state was **1115 parsed `[HYP]` blocks / 62 fingerprint slots**, not 406/29.

**What I did**
1. Reproduced the parser offline (`parse_blocks` + `fingerprint`, `github` module stubbed, no network): 1115 blocks → 62 slots.
2. Classified every block against the falsifications already recorded in `knowledge/index.md` (IDOR auth-omission, JWT alg confusion, dev-origin WAF bypass, staging `testing_*` oracles, descriptive-only classes) into4 keeps / `[PARKED]` / `[LEARN]`.
3. Applied tag-level suppression plus canonical `asset`/`class` normalization on kept blocks only.

**Result — 4 slots, 368 blocks, 0 falsified survivors**

| slot | canonical asset / class | blocks |
|---|---|---|
| `e6de2c14ee92` | `web-dev.cineplex.de` / MISCONFIG | 202 |
| `a519e53df97f` | `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/graphql` / MISCONFIG | 105 |
| `0c3a6747db5d` | `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de` / BUSLOGIC | 37 |
| `f5a92ad2c45c` | `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/` / MISCONFIG | 24 |

Two things the post-hoc slot dump caught that the plan hadn't:
- **Root cause of the 62→29 fragmentation:** `fingerprint()` hashes only asset+class, so introspection and CORS were sharing *one* 81-block slot — two distinct findings hidden inside a single issue. Fixed by writing the path into `asset` (`/graphql` vs `/`), which `norm_asset` preserves.
- **Classifier false positive:** matching `takeover` had swept 75 `testing_getConfirmationCode` account-takeover blocks into the dangle slot. Narrowed to `cname|subdomain takeover|dangl`; those75 correctly moved to `[PARKED]`.

Diff is tag/`class`/`asset` lines only (verified:0 other changed lines), `scripts/sync-issues.py` untouched. `leads/lead-bigpickle.md:7846`'s malformed attribute is now inside a `[LEARN]` block, so it is inert — recorded rather than edited. Rationale and both lessons appended to `knowledge/index.md`.

Not committed. Uncommitted so you can review; `git checkout -- leads/` reverts. Note the publisher would still open ~4 fresh issues on first sync, and pre-existing mirrored issues likely need manual closure — the parser can't see those.
