## Objective
- Continue the Cineplex API POC (`phase=POC`, `target=api`) and produce the required evidence-backed triage blocks for `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.

## Important Details
- Scope is limited to Cineplex-owned infrastructure; use only non-intrusive, read-only requests at `<=1 rps`.
- Live verification is restricted to GET/HEAD/OPTIONS; do not execute mutations, bypass authentication, or access customer/employee/financial/authentication data.
- Explicitly out of scope: DoS/lockout, descriptive-only errors/headers, TLS best practice, logout/anonymous-form CSRF, username enumeration, known-vulnerable-library-only reports, public login panels, scanner-only output, and similar excluded classes.
- Required output: one-line `[NEW]/[CHANGED]` deltas, `[PRIO]`, at most three strict-schema `[HYP]` blocks, `[PARKED]/[FINAL]`, exactly one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, and `[RISK]`.
- Priority formula: `0.25*attack_surface + 0.25*business_value + 0.15*tech_exposure + 0.15*gate_ease + 0.10*cloud_surface + 0.10*freshness`.
- `knowledge/index.md` canonical status supersedes duplicated historical and lead-tail claims. The current lead tail is malformed and still contains stale IDOR hypotheses.
- Automated harness evidence is unreliable: malformed trailing-backtick URLs cause 400, urllib UA causes Cloudflare 403, and DoH failures have repeatedly come from malformed/header defects.
- Do not infer authorization omission from `INVALID_ID` versus `UNAUTHENTICATED`; that only establishes decoder position.

## Work State
### Completed
- GraphQL introspection manually verified unauthenticated on `/` and `/graphql` for production and staging: 83 active Query and 140 active Mutation fields; 385 types, including 44 `INPUT_OBJECT` types.
- Retracted the earlier “no injection vectors” claim after deeper reads found URL/credential-shaped arguments, mass-assignment inputs, and auth-sensitive mutations.
- Production CORS verified: `/` reflects `http://localhost:3000`, `https://app.staging.cineplex.de`, and `null` with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.
- `OPTIONS /` returns 204 with `Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE,OPTIONS` and `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: content-type,authorization`; this proves browser permission for credentialed POST, but not that an ambient Cineplex cookie is usable.
- `POST /` executes GraphQL; no business mutation was executed. `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, and `/gql` are GET-only read mirrors whose POST/OPTIONS requests return API Gateway 403 `MissingAuthenticationTokenException`.
- The former “four equivalent GraphQL transports” claim was corrected: GET equivalence did not imply POST equivalence.
- Original systemic IDOR claim was falsified. A valid public cinema ID on `contentSectionListByNameAndCinemas` returned `UNAUTHENTICATED` at `selectedCinemaIdsDb`, proving an authorization check exists.
- Residual evidence is limited to pre-auth decoder/lookup reach across 15 resolvers and four decoder contracts, including list decoding inside `Array.map`; no customer data access is proven.
- Mass-assignment structure confirmed: `CinemaOperatingCompanyData.accessRightDashboard`, `accessRightFilmStatistics`, `accessRightBonusProgram`, and `accessRightCampaigning` mirror `UserPrivileges`; `updateUser(adminCinemaOperatingCompanyIds)` and `increaseUserTestingStatus(testingStatus)` have analogous read/write mirrors.
- `web-dev.cineplex.de` CNAME remains dangling: `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io`, CNAME Status 0/TTL 300, A-follow Status 3 NXDOMAIN with Azure SOA; sole CNAME in the 14-host sweep.
- Added `## CANONICAL STATUS (2026-09-30)` to `knowledge/index.md`, partitioning LIVE/DEAD/SURVIVING/METHOD RULES.
- Publisher contamination was remediated by retagging 703 `[HYP]` blocks to `[LEARN]` across the two lead files; `scripts/sync-issues.py` publishes only `[HYP]` blocks.

### Active
- Highest-ranked hypothesis: CORS misconfiguration enabling cross-origin GraphQL POST from configured dev/staging/null origins on production `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de`, confidence 95.
