+### LIVE
+- `cors_preflight_credentialed_post` @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de — `OPTIONS /` → 204 with `ACAO` reflecting hostile origins, `ACAC: true`, `ACAM` including POST, `ACAH: content-type,authorization`. Proves a browser will permit a credentialed cross-origin POST. Ambient cookie usability is still unproven.
+- `graphql_introspection` @ graphql-api.app.{,staging.}cineplex.de — unauthenticated GET, prod and staging, no env partitioning.
+- `mass_assignment_signature` @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de — schema-level read/write mirrors only. Authorization gates UNVERIFIED. No mutation executed.
+- `dangling_cname_takeover` @ web-dev.cineplex.de — CNAME Status 0, A-follow Status 3 NXDOMAIN + Azure SOA. Claimability remains provider-side.
+
+### DEAD — do not resurrect
+- **The authorization-omission inference in the `decodePublicId`-before-gate IDOR family.** Falsified: a valid *public* cinema ID on `contentSectionListByNameAndCinemas` returns `UNAUTHENTICATED` at `selectedCinemaIdsDb`, proving a gate exists on that member. `INVALID_ID` vs `UNAUTHENTICATED` only establishes *decoder position*, never authz absence.
+- Titles asserting "GET-verified cross-tenant PII" or "cross-tenant PII dump" are doubly false: the omission is falsified, and no customer record was ever touched.
+- `4 equivalent unauthenticated GraphQL surfaces` (transport equivalence) — `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql` are GET-only read mirrors; POST/OPTIONS → API-GW 403 `MissingAuthenticationTokenException`. Only `/` accepts POST.
+- `zero POST captures implies no POST capability` — those POSTs returned 403; I read a gateway rejection as a missing capability.
+- `api_cineplex_get_bypass`, `relay_metrics`, `relay_broker_saturation`, TLS-dead hosts, username enumeration, TLS best practice, logout CSRF, descriptive errors, known-vuln-library.
+
+### SURVIVING (narrow — mechanism, not IDOR)
+- Pre-auth decoder reach: 15 resolvers, 4 decoder contracts, 2 argument shapes, incl. a list decode inside `Array.map`. A fix scoped to scalar `args.id` is incomplete. Bounded and low-impact; descriptive errors are an excluded class, so file as a mechanism note, not a standalone high-severity IDOR. Cross-tenant proof is HUMAN_ONLY and out of bounds for this engagement.
+
+### METHOD RULES
+- **Suppress by editing the block tag, not by appending a correction.** An append-only falsification loses to the claim it corrects.
+- **Assert system properties only after scoping evidence to the whole system**, and name the files read.
+- Report counts as distinct fingerprints *and* distinct underlying findings; they diverged by ~7x here.
+- Method-vary every equivalence claim about an endpoint.
+- Distinguish harness failure from server behavior; malformed URLs and default UAs are tool defects, not findings.
+- **Never report a verification as complete without reading the artifact on disk.** Three "Completed" claims this cycle were false on disk.
