## CANONICAL STATUS (appended 2026-10-02 — authoritative; supersedes any conflicting dated line above)

### SURVIVING (evidence-bearing, publishable)
- `cors_preflight_credentialed_post` @ graphql-api.app.{,staging.}cineplex.de — LIVE. Same-cycle re-verified: `OPTIONS /` → 204, `ACAO: http://localhost:3000`, `ACAC: true`, `ACAH: content-type,authorization`, `ACAM: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE` (**no OPTIONS**), 2/2 envs. Preflight proves a browser would permit a credentialed write to `/`. Impact ceiling still unverified: no ambient session cookie was tested and no mutation was executed.
- `graphql_arbitrary_path_catchall` @ graphql-api.app.{,staging.}cineplex.de — **NEW this cycle.** The GraphQL server serves the full schema under *any* unshadowed path: same-cycle `GET /zz-cpx-count-probe` and `GET /nonexistent-cpx-probe-8472` both returned 200 with introspection, on prod AND staging. There is no path routing in the Express app. `/playground`, `/graphiql`, `/sandbox` are not separate console surfaces — they return GraphQL's own `Must provide query.` (18 bytes, HTTP 400), i.e. the same catch-all.
- `graphql_introspection` @ graphql-api.app.{,staging.}cineplex.de — LIVE, same-cycle: prod 83 active queries / 140 active mutations / 385 types; staging identical; zero env partitioning.
- `decoder_error_oracle` @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de — SURVIVING at **Low**, 15 resolvers across 4 decoder contracts and 2 argument shapes reach the entity-lookup layer pre-auth and return a typed decoder error with server stack frames. This is an error/ordering oracle. It is **not** an authorization omission and must never be filed as IDOR. Published under `class: ACCESS_CONTROL`.
- `dangling_cname_takeover` @ web-dev.cineplex.de — LIVE, passive. Same-cycle DoH: CNAME Status 0 → `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io` TTL 300; A-follow Status 3 NXDOMAIN. Azure claimability is provider-side and unverified.
- `mass_assignment_mirror` @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de — schema-mirror only. `CinemaOperatingCompanyData.accessRight*`, `updateUser(adminCinemaOperatingCompanyIds)`, `increaseUserTestingStatus`. Execution gates never tested; AUTH_HELPED/HUMAN_ONLY.

### CORRECTIONS THIS CYCLE
- REJECTED my own "remediation scope = 2 paths × 2 envs" (`getonly_graphql_mirrors`, asserted 2026-09-30 and 2026-10-01). That scoped remediation by a 2-path list. Same-cycle evidence shows the exposure is **path-unbounded**: every path except the three API-Gateway-shadowed ones (`/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql` → 403 `MissingAuthenticationTokenException` with `x-amzn-requestid`) returns the full schema on GET. Fixing two paths does not fix this. Remediation must be scoped to the application (disable introspection / require auth) plus removal of the three GW routes.
- `curl --data-urlencode 'query=...'` **without `-G` issues a POST**, not a GET. My recorded recipe "urlencoded GET via curl --data-urlencode returns 200" silently became `POST` with `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` and returned `POST body missing, invalid Content-Type`. The correct form is `curl -G --data-urlencode query@file`. Same failure class as reading a gateway 403 as a missing capability: the tool's request shape, not the server's behaviour, produced the observation.
- 9,818 block headers across `leads/lead-*.md` were **fused** to the preceding attribute line with no blank-line separator. `parse_blocks` only breaks on a blank line or a `STOP` tag, so every one of those blocks absorbed the attribute lines of the block beneath it. One orphan line `class: 'MISCONFIG' conf: '93'` (11 copies) was captured whole by `KV` — everything after the first colon — and overwrote the real `class` of the block above it. Consequence: junk fingerprint `58ac107c6a91` **merged the live CORS finding, the falsified systemic IDOR, the decoder oracle and introspection into a single tracker issue slot**, so the falsified IDOR rode to the tracker *inside* the live CORS issue regardless of class-level retagging.

### PUBLISH PATH (measured by executing `scripts/sync-issues.py`'s own `parse_blocks` + `fingerprint` over `leads/lead-*.md`, 2026-10-02)
- Before → after remediation: `[HYP]` blocks **1173 → 851**; fingerprints **63 → 52**; distinct titles **251 → 184**.
- `class: IDOR` blocks **297 → 0**. The decoder oracle moved to `ACCESS_CONTROL` (11 blocks, fingerprint `4ad65631f720`); the unverified valid-JWT `adminUsers/searchUsers` claims moved to `AUTH`.
- Junk fingerprint `58ac107c6a91` now returns 0 blocks. Fixes applied: 9,818 blank-line separations, 9 orphan malformed lines removed, 287 falsified IDOR/ownership-omission blocks retagged `[LEARN]`, 29 dev-origin maintenance-exit blocks retagged `[PARKED]` (blocked, not falsified), 3 live introspection blocks restored after the first pass over-matched them.
- Still publishable but NOT evidence-backed and must not be reported: 208-block staging `testing_*` auth family, 55-block JWT alg/key-confusion family, 42-block anonymous-mutation authz-gap family. These rest on schema reads and unverified gate assumptions.

### DEAD (do not re-derive)
- `idor_booking` ownership-omission / cross-tenant PII exposure — FALSIFIED. `INVALID_ID` proves decoder ordering only. A valid public ID in `contentSectionListByNameAndCinemas` fires its gate. The "missing ownership check" inference is dead; the decoder oracle is the surviving half.
- `api.cineplex.de` GET-based GraphQL execution — REJECTED, strict 403 across all methods and encodings.
- Relay `data-9fc27eb430.cineplex.de` undocumented routes / metrics — REJECTED, descriptive endpoint map and telemetry counters.
- `getOnlineTicketingBooking` SSRF — REJECTED, root-gated.
- Staging `testing_*` confirmation-code oracle — REJECTED as a descriptive-only finding; its ATO framing needs HUMAN_ONLY and was never proven.

### SELF-NOTES
- Keyword-based suppression failed twice, in both directions. The first pass caught 287 falsified blocks that said "IDOR" and missed 14 more that asserted the same falsified thing as "authorization is omitted ahead of ID decoding" / "authorization is enforced per-resolver by hand". Then it *over*-matched 3 live introspection blocks that merely mention IDOR as downstream impact, and would have destroyed the one real Low result. Suppress on **verdict**, decided per title, never on vocabulary or on `class` alone.
- Confirming a property of a system requires running the system's own code. Every "publish path is clear" claim so far came from reading one file; the true publish set is only ever knowable by executing `parse_blocks` over the glob, and it is only ever true for the cycle in which it was measured.
