- `dev_origin_gateway_lift` — 29 blocks re-tagged to PARKED: blocked on a maintenance window, not falsified.
- `dangling_cname_takeover` @ web-dev.cineplex.de — same-cycle DoH confirms CNAME Status 0 → `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io` TTL 300, A-follow Status 3 NXDOMAIN. Report-ready but claimability is provider-side; unverified, so it stays conditional.

[FINAL]
- Reportable now: **2 Medium/High findings** (path-unbounded introspection; credentialed-CORS write primitive) plus **1 Low** (decoder oracle). Nothing else in the corpus is evidence-backed.
- Do **not** submit from the corpus: the 208-block staging `testing_*` auth family, the 55-block JWT alg/key-confusion family, and the 42-block anonymous-mutation authorization-gap family. All three rest on schema reads and unverified gate assumptions; they are hypotheses, not findings.
- On disk this cycle: `leads/lead-bigpickle.md` and `leads/lead-nemotron3.md` received 9,818 blank-line block separations, 9 orphan malformed attribute lines removed, 287 falsified IDOR/ownership-omission blocks re-tagged `[LEARN]`, 29 dev-origin blocks re-tagged `[PARKED]`, 3 live introspection blocks restored, and 11 decoder-oracle blocks moved to `ACCESS_CONTROL`. `knowledge/index.md` gained an authoritative CANONICAL STATUS section. 0 fused headers remain.

[NEXT]
PROBE: establish whether the API-Gateway shadowing applies to POST as well, which decides whether the credentialed-write primitive is reachable under any path or only under `/`:
`curl -sS -m 20 --http2 -A "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/126.0 Safari/537.36" -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Origin: http://localhost:3000" --data '{"query":"{__typename}"}' -D - "https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/zz-cpx-post-probe"` then the same against `/graphql` as control. A pure query, no mutation, one request per path.

[LEARN]
- `parse_blocks` stops only on a blank line or a `STOP` tag. 9,818 headers had no preceding blank line, so blocks absorbed the attribute lines of the block beneath them, and one orphan `class: 'MISCONFIG' conf: '93'` line was captured whole by the `KV` regex and overwrote the real class of the block above it. Fixing the tag was never going to be enough — the parser needed the corpus to be well-formed.
- Keyword-based suppression failed in both directions in one pass. It caught 287 blocks that said "IDOR" and missed 14 asserting the identical falsified claim as "authorization is omitted ahead of ID decoding", then over-matched 3 live introspection blocks that mention IDOR only as downstream impact. Suppress on verdict, decided per title; never on vocabulary or on `class` alone.
- `curl --data-urlencode 'query=...'` without `-G` sends a POST. My recorded recipe for "urlencoded GET returns 200" silently became a form POST and returned `POST body missing`. Correct form is `curl -G --data-urlencode query@file`. Same class of error as reading a gateway 403 as a missing capability — the tool's request shape produced the observation, not the server.
- I have twice generalised equivalence from one dimension:2026-09-28, GET-body equivalence generalized to transport, and this cycle, a 2-path list generalized from three shadowed paths to the whole surface. Vary the dimension you are about to generalize over.

[RISK]
- **Medium** — publish path: 851 blocks / 52 fingerprints remain publishable while only 2 fingerprints are evidence-backed. Roughly 305 blocks across the staging auth, JWT and anonymous-mutation families would reach a human reviewer as findings on schema-read-only evidence. Nothing in the publisher distinguishes "measured" from "assumed".
- **Medium** — reporting risk on CORS: the preflight is proven, the impact is not. Any write-up implying account takeover or a confirmed data read from this evidence would be rejected.
- **Low** — the corpus still rewrites itself every cycle. Counts here are true only for this cycle and must be re-measured by executing the parser, not by reading a summary.
