## Objective
- Continue the Cineplex Deutschland bug bounty hunt by validating and consolidating the highest-value GraphQL/business-logic findings (credentialed CORS primitive, mass assignment, IDOR chaining/decoder reach, dual GraphQL entry points) while avoiding program out-of-scope classes and correcting the known `probe-results.md` harness bias.

## Important Details
- **Program**: Cineplex Deutschland GmbH & Co. KG / Cineplex Group (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu)
- **Scope**: company-owned infrastructure, websites, ticketing systems, mobile applications, APIs, customer portals, loyalty platforms, digital signage systems, and domains operated by Cineplex Deutschland GmbH & Co. KG and participating Cineplex entities under its control (see `scope.yml` + `inventory/cineplex.md`)
- **Out-of-scope (explicit)**: network DoS/account-lockout DoS, descriptive errors/headers only, robots.txt/known public files, outdated library versions, OPTIONS/TRACE, CSRF on logout/anonymous forms, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, self-XSS, scanner reports without POC, physical access, social engineering, username enumeration on login/forgot-password, brute-force/rate-limit/lockout policy, SSL/TLS best practice/attacks, clickjacking without demonstrated exploit, mail config (SPF/DKIM/DMARC), known-vulnerable library without program-specific exploit, password/account-recovery policy, autocomplete, public login panels, lack of email verification, session control during email/password change, exposure of customer/employee/financial/authentication data during testing
- **Harness defect (`.github/workflows/hunt.yml:207–225`)**: URL regex/`strip()` omit backtick -> literal trailing `` ` `` produces HTTP 400; `User-Agent: ... (passive verifier)` hits Cloudflare bot-gate -> HTTP 403; `urls[:12]` truncates candidates. `probe-results.md` is therefore not reliable for POST, `/graphql`, arbitrary-path, or balanced GET evidence. Trust manual `curl --http2` with balanced URL-encoded `?query=...` and a browser UA.
- **GraphQL surfaces**: `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de` and `graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de` expose full introspection (prod 83 Query + 140 Mutation, staging 83 Query identical). Both `/` and `/graphql` are unauthenticated and return identical schema/IDOR surface. `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql` are GET-only mirrors (API-GW 403 on POST/OPTIONS). Root `/` accepts CORS preflight + POST execution.
- **CORS (prod root `/`)**: `OPTIONS /` 204 reflects `Origin` into `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`, `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`, `Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE`, `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: content-type,authorization`. Observed reflected origins include `http://localhost:3000`, `https://app.staging.cineplex.de`, `null`. Disallowed origins throw `Error: Not allowed by CORS` from `/var/task/graphql.js:47459:17` (500). Credentialed mutation primitive exists but requires an ambient authenticated browser session.
- **IDOR/decoder reach**: 4 single-entity resolvers (`userById`, `invoice`, `order`, `ticket`) decode-before-gate (`decodePublicId`) -> `200 INVALID_ID` with no `Authorization`; `currentUser` -> `200 UNAUTHENTICATED` on same surface. Chaining: `ticket(id)->order->user`, `order(id)->user`. `userByQr(qrCode)` returns `User`. `User` has 51 fields including `onlineTicketingToken`, `inviteCode`, `linkedAccounts`, blocked fields, and financial history. 6/6 sibling gates fire (e.g. `searchUsers` ROLE, `adminUsers` ROOT, `userByQr` DEVICE, `voucherInstanceByQR` POS, `errorStatistics` UNAUTHENTICATED).
- **Mass assignment / auth-layer primitives**: `CinemaOperatingCompanyData` has `accessRightDashboard/FilmStatistics/BonusProgram/Campaigning` + `cinemasIds` mirroring `UserPrivileges`. `updateUser(userId:ID!, ..., adminCinemaOperatingCompanyIds:[ID!], resetAppChangeBlockedUntil:Boolean)`. `increaseUserTestingStatus(testingStatus: TestingStatus!)`. `login(email,password,privileged:Boolean,...)`, `refreshLogin(refreshToken,privileged:Boolean)`, `loginPOS(authToken:String!)`. `sendNotifications(authToken:String!, userIds:[ID!], ...)`. `deleteCineplexUser(id:String!, apiKey:String!)`. `storeSDKLogin(data:{cookieId,userId,...})`, `storeConsent(data:{cookieId,...})`, `logItems(...)`, `editUserGroupFilter(id:ID!, ...)`. `updatePassword` deprecated with nullable credential args.
- **Dangling CNAME**: `web-dev.cineplex.de` CNAME -> `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io` with A-follow `Status 3 NXDOMAIN` + Azure SOA (machine-checkable via DoH `Accept: application/dns-json`) — 17th+ consecutive cycle. Sole dangle in swept sets.
- **Dev origin surface**: `buchung-dev.cineplex.de` and `bms-dev.cineplex.de` on `194.77.169.121` (direct origin, no Cloudflare) — SPAs live; `/gateway/*` routes oscillate between 200/503/403 depending on cycle. `booking-dev.cineplex.de` is ingress default-backend (404). `dev.cineplex.de` A 10.20.0.7 (RFC1918) — info only.
- **Relay**: `data-9fc27eb430.cineplex.de` `/health` 200 + `/metrics` 200 (IOMB broker stats) — descriptive infra only; queue telemetry growing but no exploitable authless manipulation path.
- **Knowledge base state**: `knowledge/index.md` has `## CANONICAL STATUS (2026-09-30)` (LIVE/DEAD/SURVIVING/METHOD RULES). Publisher `scripts/sync-issues.py` uses `[HYP]` blocks from `leads/lead-*.md`. Residual falsified IDOR text was suppressed from publish path by tag/class rules; `decoder_error_oracle` retained as `ACCESS_CONTROL` (Low). Harness defects documented.
- **Inventory baseline**: `inventory/cineplex.md` — 132 hosts (confirmed complete as of 2026-09-23). CT diff + CNAME sweep exhausted.

