## Objective
- Continue the Cineplex bug-hunt in `POC` phase for target `api`, validate only high-value scoped findings, and emit the required structured blocks.
- Prioritize passive-first, same-cycle evidence while avoiding rejected classes and live customer-data mutations.

## Important Details
- Canonical survivors: CORS credentialed cross-origin write primitive (88), mass assignment on privilege fields (85), dangling Azure Container Apps domain (72).
- CORS: `OPTIONS /` on both `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de` and `graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de` returns `204`, reflected `ACAO`, `ACAC: true`, `ACAH: content-type,authorization`, and `ACAM: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE`; `OPTIONS` is not in `ACAM`. Root `/` is POST-capable. Actual authenticated browser impact remains `AUTH_HELPED`.
- CORS allowlist includes `http://localhost:3000` and `https://app.staging.cineplex.de` on production; the staging-origin trust is the practical cross-environment pairing.
- GraphQL exposes the full schema through root and any unshadowed path; remediation scope is a path pattern across both environments, not four named routes. `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, and `/gql` are GET-only API Gateway mirrors; POST/OPTIONS return `403 MissingAuthenticationTokenException`.
- GraphQL schema evidence: 83 active queries, 140 active mutations, 385 types, 44 `INPUT_OBJECT` types; introspection is supporting evidence, not currently a standalone report.
- Mass-assignment evidence: `CinemaOperatingCompanyData.accessRight*` mirrors derived `UserPrivileges`; `updateUser(adminCinemaOperatingCompanyIds, resetAppChangeBlockedUntil)` and `increaseUserTestingStatus` remain unexecuted pending a consented sandbox account.
- Dangling CNAME: `web-dev.cineplex.de` → `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io`; CNAME Status 0 TTL 300, target A Status 3 NXDOMAIN with Azure SOA. Azure-side claimability and mapping release remain unverified.
- Retraction: the systemic IDOR is falsified. A valid public cinema ID against `contentSectionListByNameAndCinemas` returned `UNAUTHENTICATED`; `INVALID_ID` versus `UNAUTHENTICATED` proves decoder position, not missing ownership. Do not republish the IDOR claim.
- Retracted/downgraded claims: “four equivalent GraphQL transports,” “two paths × two environments” for named routes, `getOnlineTicketingBooking` SSRF, staging `testing_getConfirmationCode` oracle, and standalone introspection scoring.
- `probe-results.md` is not authoritative: current probe URLs can contain trailing backticks, use a bot-identifying urllib UA, and truncate candidates. Use balanced URL encoding and direct same-cycle reads.
- Program exclusions remain active: username enumeration, TLS best practices, logout CSRF, descriptive errors/headers, known-vulnerable libraries without exploit, DoS, scanner-only claims, and customer-data exposure.
- Live work must remain passive-first, ≤1 rps, and limited to read-only requests; no live mutations or cross-tenant customer-data access.

