The test surfaced a **5th, unrecorded defect**: `}` is excluded from the URL charset, so every GraphQL verification URL is emitted as `?query={__typename` — malformed, which would 400 and be misread as "endpoint dead". Fixing that too:
[0m$ [0mcd /home/runner/work/cineplex-hunt/cineplex-hunt && python3 - <<'EOF'
import re
pat=re.compile(r'https?://[^\s"\)\]]+')
def fix(m):
    u=m.strip('.,;)]>`') if '{' in m else m.strip('.,;)]}>`')
    if u.count('{')>u.count('}'):
        u=u.rstrip('.,;')+('}'*(u.count('{')-u.count('}')))
    return u
sample='''`OPTIONS https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/` -> 204
catch-all https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/totally/unknown/path/xyz?query={__typename}` -> 200
multi-field https://g.cineplex.de/q?query={cinemas{id} shows{id}}` -> 200
bare trailing brace https://ex.com/a} end
wrapped (https://web-dev.cineplex.de/) [https://ex.com/x] "https://q.example/z"
https://plain.example/a, next'''
seen=[]
for m in pat.findall(sample):
    u=fix(m)
    if u.startswith('https://') and u not in seen: seen.append(u)
for u in seen: print('OK ',u)
EOF
