## Objective
- Continue the Cineplex Phase POC/triage workflow for target `api`, producing the requested 8-step structured analyst output.
- Prioritize the three surviving hypotheses and obtain the first trustworthy automated verifier coverage after harness repairs.

## Important Details
- Scope: Cineplex-owned assets only; avoid customer/employee/auth data and mutating live data.
- Rejected classes include descriptive-only findings, TLS/SSL, logout CSRF, username enumeration, known-vulnerable-library-only reports, DoS, and similar exclusions.
- Final survivor ranking: credentialed CORS write primitive (88), privilege-field mass assignment (85), dangling CNAME (72).
- CORS evidence: production reflects `http://localhost:3000` and `https://app.staging.cineplex.de` with `ACAC: true`; `OPTIONS /` returns 204, exact `ACAM: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE`, and permits `content-type,authorization`. Root `/` is POST-capable; credentialed impact remains `AUTH_HELPED`.
- GraphQL serves introspection/schema under root, named GET mirrors, and any unshadowed catch-all path; `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql` reject POST/OPTIONS at API Gateway.
- The prior systemic IDOR authorization-omission claim is falsified. Only a Low pre-auth decoder/error oracle survives and should not be published.
- Mass-assignment evidence is schema-level and not execution-verified; use only a consented sandbox/test-owned object.
- `web-dev.cineplex.de` remains a dangling Azure Container Apps CNAME; DNS NXDOMAIN is proven, but provider claimability attestation is outstanding.
- Do not re-derive the closed harness or publisher defects next cycle. Prior automated-log absence/403/400 conclusions are inadmissible.
- Live probes must remain passive-first, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, browser UA, and ≤1 rps.

## Work State
### Completed
- Fixed all seven verifier defects in `.github/workflows/hunt.yml`; YAML and embedded Python compile.
- Verifier now extracts 414 in-scope candidates across 67 hosts, skips 192 out-of-scope hosts, records explicit probe/truncation counts, rejects placeholders, and round-robins hosts.
- Added `PROBE_HOSTS`, `PROBE_MAX=240`, zero-glob `SystemExit`, corrected URL cleanup/encoding, and browser UA.
- Added post-suppression near-duplicate collapse in `scripts/sync-issues.py`; affected assets are unioned rather than dropped.
- Fixed `ensure_label()` in `scripts/sync-issues.py:153` to return the GitHub label object.
- Verified publisher offline: 1224 blocks → 70 fingerprints → 59 after retraction suppression → 57 after near-duplicate collapse; repeated runs are idempotent and all three survivors remain.
- Confirmed candidate extraction includes CORS root, catch-all GraphQL GET, and `web-dev.cineplex.de`.
- Added canonical LIVE/DEAD/SURVIVING/METHOD status to `knowledge/index.md`; later retagging removed falsified IDOR blocks from the publish path.

### Active
- First honest live verifier cycle has not yet run after the seven fixes.
- Breadth remains sparse: `graphql-api.app.{,staging.}cineplex.de` dominate prior analysis while roughly 60 of 67 in-scope hosts are lightly examined.
- Lead-authoring debt remains: multiple `web-dev` blocks use divergent classes/titles, and two blocks have malformed class metadata.

### Blocked
- CORS credentialed impact requires an authenticated browser round trip on a consented test account/object.
- Mass assignment execution requires a consented sandbox account.
- Dangling-CNAME impact requires Azure-side confirmation that the Container App/custom-domain mapping is reclaimable.
- No automated cycle can validate those human/provider-gated impacts.

