## Objective
- Continue the authorized Cineplex Group bug-bounty engagement in `POC` phase, target `api`, using the latest evidence to emit only the required Step 1–7 structured blocks with at most three hypotheses and one next action.
- Preserve superseding corrections; do not revive the falsified IDOR claim or obsolete schema conclusions.

## Important Details
- Scope: Cineplex Deutschland GmbH & Co. KG / Cineplex Group company-owned assets from `scope.yml` and `inventory/cineplex.md`; report channel is `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Live testing is passive-first, ≤1 rps, and limited to `GET`/`HEAD`/`OPTIONS`; no autonomous mutations, authentication bypass, customer PII, or account-recovery testing.
- Reject DoS/lockout, descriptive errors/headers, username enumeration, TLS best practices, CSRF logout/anonymous forms, mail configuration, known-vulnerable-library-only findings, scanner-only claims, public login/version disclosures, and similar explicit exclusions.
- Strongest current surface: `https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/` and `https://graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de/`; full unauthenticated schema has 83 active queries, 140 active mutations, 385 types, and 44 `INPUT_OBJECT` types.
- Any unshadowed GraphQL path serves introspection, e.g. `GET /totally/unknown/path/xyz?query={__typename}` → `200 {"data":{"__typename":"Query"}}`.
- Root `/` is the credentialed POST/CORS route; `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, and `/gql` are GET-only API-Gateway mirrors whose POST/OPTIONS return `403 MissingAuthenticationTokenException`.
- CORS preflight on `/` returns `204`, reflected `ACAO`, `ACAC: true`, `ACAM: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE`, and `ACAH: content-type,authorization`. `OPTIONS` is not in observed `ACAM`.
