class: MISCONFIG
asset: graphql-api.app.cineplex.de, graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de
confidence: 86
reasoning: Confirmed live on the actual response, not preflight only. Prod reflects a credentialed ACAO for `https://sub.attacker.cineplex.de` (200, ACAC:true) and for `Origin: null` (200, ACAC:true, real data); staging reflects `Origin: null` identically. The allowlist is not blind reflection, and it is not a naive `endsWith` bug: `evilcineplex.de`, `notcineplex.de` and `a.evilcineplex.de` all return 500 with no CORS headers, so the match requires a label boundary. That boundary check is a genuine mitigation against lookalike registrable domains and it is why this cycle's confidence drops from 88 — the primitive is real but the attacker must control a genuine `*.cineplex.de` hostname. ACAO is issued without any DNS resolution of the origin, so a dangling or unclaimed subdomain is sufficient to be trusted.
evidence_needed: A consented test account plus a page served from a trusted origin the tester controls, showing a credentialed cross-origin request reaching GraphQL and returning data; SameSite cookie attributes shown not to block it; and a harmless test-owned mutation succeeding under a victim session cookie.
verify_steps: Executed read-only this cycle: `curl -X OPTIONS https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/ -H 'Origin: https://sub.attacker.cineplex.de' -H 'Access-Control-Request-Method: POST' -H 'Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type,authorization'` (204, reflected, ACAC true); `curl -H 'Origin: https://sub.attacker.cineplex.de' 'https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/?query={__typename}'` (200, reflected, ACAC true). Human-gated remainder: from a page on a controlled trusted origin, `fetch(..., {credentials:'include'})` against prod GraphQL with an authenticated test session.
impact: An attacker controlling any single `*.cineplex.de` hostname can issue credentialed cross-origin reads and writes against both the production and staging GraphQL APIs in a victim's browser, riding that victim's session, and can additionally use `Origin: null` from sandboxed iframes or `file://`. Escalates to cross-environment privilege and vertical privilege escalation when combined with the mass-assignment surface.
testability: AUTH_HELPED
