## Objective
- Continue the Cineplex API POC (`phase: POC`, `target: api`) and produce only the required structured analyst blocks, centered on GraphQL CORS, mass assignment, and the `web-dev.cineplex.de` takeover chain.

## Important Details
- Stay within Cineplex-owned assets; use read-only probes at ≤1 rps, no customer/PII access, no autonomous mutations, and avoid all explicitly rejected classes.
- Trust same-cycle manual `curl`/DNS captures; `probe-results.md` is currently unusable because the verifier’s globs match nothing, so all 204 prior automated cycles are considered void.
- CORS allowlist uses a DNS label boundary, not a raw string suffix: `cineplex.de` and genuine `*.cineplex.de` hosts are trusted; `evilcineplex.de`, `notcineplex.de`, `a.evilcineplex.de`, and `cineplex.de.evil.com` are rejected.
- Production actual GraphQL responses reflect trusted origins, including non-resolving `*.cineplex.de` and `Origin: null`, with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`; staging also trusts `Origin: null`.
- Root `OPTIONS /` on both environments returns 204 with reflected ACAO, `ACAC: true`, `ACAM: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE` (no `OPTIONS`), and `ACAH: content-type,authorization`. Browser victim-session impact remains unproven.
- GraphQL introspection is exposed under any unshadowed path on both environments. Root `/` is POST-capable; `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, and `/gql` are GET-only API-GW mirrors.
- Mass assignment is schema-confirmed but execution-unproven: `CinemaOperatingCompanyData` contains four `accessRight*` flags plus `cinemasIds`; `updateUser` accepts `adminCinemaOperatingCompanyIds` and `resetAppChangeBlockedUntil`. `UserPrivileges` is an `OBJECT` with `inputFields: null`, not an input object.
- The former 4/4 IDOR claim is falsified. `INVALID_ID` versus `UNAUTHENTICATED` proves decoder ordering, not a missing ownership check; retain only a low-severity decoder oracle.
- `web-dev.cineplex.de` CNAMEs to `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io`; the target is NXDOMAIN. Azure claimability is unattested and must not be tested without authorization.
- Current survivors: `cors_credentialed_crossenv_graphql` (86, `MISCONFIG`, `AUTH_HELPED`), `mass_assignment_privilege_fields` (85, `BUSLOGIC`, `AUTH_HELPED`), and `dangling_cname_webdev` (74, `OTHER`, `HUMAN_ONLY`).

