## Objective
- Act as senior bug-bounty analyst for Cineplex program (report channel bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running an 8-step per-cycle hunt loop producing only structured blocks ([PRIO]/[HYP]/[PARKED]/[FINAL]/[NEXT]/[LEARN]/[RISK]).
- Current phase: POC, target `api`; top findings are CORS credentialed trust, mass-assignment, and web-dev dangling CNAME chain.

## Important Details
- In-scope: only Cineplex-owned infra per scope.yml + inventory/cineplex.md; read-only passive-first probes, ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; no mutating tests on live customer data.
- REJECTED classes (explicit exclusions): username_enumeration, ssl_tls_best_practices, csrf_logout, descriptive_errors (incl. 500s/stacktraces), known_vuln_library, OAuth/JWKS passive paths, relay_metrics/relay_broker_saturation (descriptive IOMB infra), api.cineplex.de GET-bypass (dead), TLS-dead hosts (app.staging, graphql-api.app.couat, login, sso), relay/metrics.
- Harness defect: retired inline verifier in `.github/workflows/hunt.yml:207-225` corrupted all 206 cycles (trailing backtick → 400, UA `(passive verifier)` → WAF 403, `urls[:12]` truncation, brace truncation). Replaced by `scripts/passive_verify.py` with 14 offline tests (`scripts/test_passive_verify.py`). All automated-log-derived conclusions are void; live evidence = manual balanced `curl -G --data-urlencode` with browser UA.
- CORS allowlist matches `*.cineplex.de` with a DNS label boundary (evilcineplex.de/notcineplex.de/a.evilcineplex.de → 500; sub.attacker.cineplex.de → 204), reflects `ACAC: true`, `Origin: null` credentialed, no DNS resolution of origin. `ACAM` observed = `GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE` (NO OPTIONS entry). Hostile prod entries: `http://localhost:3000`, `https://app.staging.cineplex.de`.
- Only `POST /` accepts credentialed POST + executes GraphQL; `/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql` are GET-only mirrors (API-GW 403 `MissingAuthenticationTokenException`); arbitrary unshadowed paths serve schema (catch-all) → remediation is path-pattern × 2 envs.
- `idor_booking` falsified: `INVALID_ID` vs `UNAUTHENTICATED` measures decode position, not check presence (falsified by `contentSectionListByNameAndCinemas` returning UNAUTHENTICATED). Survives: pre-auth decoder reach (15 resolvers, 4 decoder contracts, 2 arg shapes). Falsified IDOR `class: IDOR` blocks cleared 297→0 in publish path; decoder oracle retained as `class: ACCESS_CONTROL` (fingerprint `4ad65631f720`).
- Publisher `scripts/sync-issues.py`: `parse_blocks` matches `^\[HYP]` only (line 57), globs `leads/lead-*.md`; fingerprint = md5(asset|class); offline mock run: 1224 blocks → 70 fingerprints → 59 after retraction suppression → 57 after near-dup collapse; idempotent; `CLOSE_SUPPRESSED=1` behavior documented. Known debt: web-dev dangle authored as ~5 divergent-class [HYP] blocks (not auto-mergeable), 2 blocks with malformed class `'MISCONFIG' CONF: '93'`.
- Correctness rules earned: a type isn't "read" until its field list is in hand; method-vary every equivalence claim; scope system claims to files actually read; label-boundary controls required for suffix-allowlist claims; no unverified completeness assertions (4 self-error instances recorded 2026-09-26).
