- 2026-10-05 Remaining tracker debt, NOT auto-mergeable and deliberately left alone: the single web-dev dangling-CNAME root cause is still authored as ~5 separate [HYP] blocks carrying divergent class labels (MISCONFIG / OTHER / SUBDOMAIN_TAKEOVER) and materially different titles, so title-similarity collapse correctly refuses to merge them (titles differ well past 0.82 and classes disagree). Merging across differing class labels would destroy taxonomy signal, so this is lead-authoring discipline to fix at the source, not a publisher change. Also 2 blocks carry a malformed class value `'MISCONFIG' CONF: '93'` from inline-attribute splitting — cosmetic, class-normalization debt.
- 2026-10-05 ACCEPTED cors_label_boundary_semantics @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: a suffix-style CORS allowlist is only exploitable if the accepted pattern is checked for a label boundary. Three live controls (`evilcineplex.de`, `notcineplex.de`, `a.evilcineplex.de` all 500 vs `sub.attacker.cineplex.de` 204) distinguish a DNS-correct suffix match from a naive `endsWith` bug, and the correct-semantics result is the one that must be recorded. Any future suffix-allowlist claim needs registrable-domain controls before the impact statement is written.
- 2026-10-05 ACCEPTED cors_resolvability_irrelevant @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: the credentialed ACAO is issued for origins that do not resolve, since the allowlist is evaluated on the Origin string before any DNS lookup. Practical exploitation still requires the attacker to actually serve script from a trusted origin, so this is a primitive-strength fact rather than an exploit on its own.
- 2026-10-05 Measured publisher behaviour end-to-end against a mock GitHub (offline, no network): 1224 blocks -> 70 fingerprints -> 59 after retraction suppression -> 57 after near-duplicate collapse; two consecutive runs stay at 57 with zero duplicate creates (idempotent); CLOSE_SUPPRESSED=1 closes and labels a pre-existing open retracted issue, default leaves it open. All three survivors confirmed present in the final published set.
