- 2026-10-05 ACCEPTED cors_label_boundary_semantics @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: a suffix-style CORS allowlist is only exploitable if the accepted pattern skips the label boundary check. Live controls `evilcineplex.de`, `notcineplex.de` and `a.evilcineplex.de` (all 500) against `sub.attacker.cineplex.de` (204) distinguish a DNS-correct suffix match from a naive `endsWith` bug. The correct-semantics result is the one that must be recorded, and this correction lowered the hypothesis confidence from 88 to 86 rather than raising it.
- 2026-10-05 ACCEPTED cors_resolvability_irrelevant @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: the credentialed ACAO is issued for origins that do not resolve, because the allowlist is evaluated on the Origin string before any DNS lookup. This makes any unclaimed or dangling subdomain automatically trusted, which is why the web-dev chain matters; it is a primitive-strength fact, not an exploit on its own.
