IDOR gates: userById/order/ticket/invoice return INVALID_ID with decodePublicId stacktrace for non-existent/invalid IDs (no auth). userByQr → DEVICE_UNAUTHORIZED. Controls: currentUser UNAUTHENTICATED, searchUsers requires roles, adminUsers root-only, voucherInstanceByQR POS-only, errorStatistics auth-gated. Chaining fields exist conceptually but no arbitrary public ID yields user data without valid related ID; using random/invalid IDs only triggers decode gate (no cross-tenant read observed). Safe mapping only with public non-PII IDs (cinemas) - no customer PII touched.

Infra: web-dev CNAME→AzureContainerApps; DoH shows A follow returns NXDOMAIN+SOA (dangling). bms-dev 200 at root (SPA), some gateway paths 200; buchung-dev root 403/varies; dev 10.20.0.7 RFC1918. graphql-api endpoints return full schema on / and /graphql (catch-all) with browser UA; automated verifier UA behavior remains invalid as evidence.

1) CORS end-to-end verified for specified cases (OPTIONS+GET, both paths where possible, prod+staging). 2) Decoder-vs-gate boundary observed; no arbitrary public ID chaining to user PII using invalid IDs (safe test). 3) web-dev DoH confirmed CNAME + A-follow NXDOMAIN (machine-verifiable). Next: test with any real public-order/ticket IDs only if they exist and without PII, or hold as HUMAN_ONLY per rules.
