## Confirmed findings

- **CORS on actual POST (arbitrary origin):** `POST https://graphql-api.app.cineplex.de/` with `Origin: https://attacker.cineplex.de` and `Content-Type: application/json` returns `ACAO: https://attacker.cineplex.de`, `ACAC: true`, HTTP 200, and `{"data":{"__typename":"Query"}}`. Adding `Authorization: dummy` does not change reflection (`ACAO` + `ACAC:true` still present).
- **CORS preflight + actual both reflective:** Production GraphQL API reflects arbitrary origins on preflight and on actual responses while allowing credentials. For observed allowlisted origins (`http://localhost:3000`, `https://app.staging.cineplex.de`) same `ACAC:true` on actual responses.
- **GraphQL catchall:** Arbitrary unshadowed paths on prod and staging return `{"data":{"__typename":"Query"}}` (schema surface reachable beyond named routes).
- **Dangling CNAME:** `web-dev.cineplex.de` CNAME -> `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io.` (Status 0). Target A lookup returns `Status 3` (NXDOMAIN) with Azure SOA. Persistent precondition.

## Learnings
- `cors_actual_post_reflected_arbitrary_origin` @ graphql-api.app.cineplex.de: Actual credentialed-allowed responses reflect arbitrary origin on POST to `/` (primitive confirmed via read-only observations).
- Configuration is consistent across preflight and actual responses for the tested cases.

## Impact/limits (read-only)
- Browser-based cross-origin requests with credentials could be sent if ambient auth exists. Demonstrating credentialed data read requires a controlled browser context and an existing session (HUMAN_ONLY per rules). No mutations attempted.

## No further safe passive steps
All requested read-only checks (CORS preflight/actual, arbitrary paths, DoH CNAME/A) are complete. No obvious additional passive probes (≤1 rps, read-only) without moving toward PoC.

