## Important Details
- **Program Scope:** All company-owned infrastructure, websites, ticketing systems, mobile applications, APIs, customer portals, loyalty platforms, digital signage systems, and domains operated by Cineplex Deutschland GmbH & Co. KG and participating entities under its control.
- **High-Priority Classes:** Broken auth/session, IDOR/BOLA, SSRF-to-cloud-metadata (169.254.169.254), mass assignment, JWT alg/key confusion, OAuth redirect_uri/state flaws, business logic on money/auth flows, file upload, GraphQL introspection+mutations, and subdomain takeover.
- **Explicitly Out-of-Scope:** DoS, account-lockout DoS, descriptive errors/headers only, robots.txt/known public files, SSL/TLS best practices/attacks, CSRF on logout/anonymous forms, username enumeration on login/forgot-password, brute-force/rate-limit/lockout policy, known-vulnerable libraries without a program-specific exploit, and any exposure of customer/employee/financial/authentication data during testing.
- **Testing Constraints:** <=1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only for live probes, passive-first, no auth-bypass or mutating tests against live customer data, and all claims must be traceable to manual read-only verification (automated log is harness-defective).
- **Known Harness Defect:** `.github/workflows/hunt.yml` probe runner is broken (trailing backtick in URLs, `(passive verifier)` User-Agent triggering WAF 403 bot-gate, brace truncation causing false-negative 400s, and truncated URL lists). `probe-results.md` (current 1330+ lines) contains zero POST GraphQL probes and cannot be used as negative evidence. Manual `curl` with a browser User-Agent is required.
- **Top Live Findings:**
  - **graphql-api.app.{cineplex.de, staging.cineplex.de}:** Unauthenticated GraphQL introspection confirmed (83 queries, 140 mutations, 385 types, 44 INPUT_OBJECTs) on `/` and `/graphql` (both GET-capable for reads, only `/` accepts POST). Arbitrary unshadowed paths also serve the schema. 
  - **CORS Misconfiguration:** On `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de`, `OPTIONS /` returns 204 with `ACAO` reflected, `ACAC: true`, `ACAM: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE`, `ACAH: content-type,authorization` for `null`, `http://localhost:3000`, and `https://app.staging.cineplex.de`. The allowlist enforces DNS label boundary (not raw suffix) and returns ACAO+ACAC:true on actual responses.
  - **IDOR Structure:** 4/4 resolvers (`userById`, `invoice`, `order`, `ticket`) decode before auth on `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de`; chaining (`ticket(id)->order->user`, `order(id)->user`) and `userByQr(qrCode)` reach the 51-field `User` object. 6/6 sibling gates fire correctly (`currentUser`, `searchUsers`, `adminUsers`, `userByQr`, `voucherInstanceByQR`, `errorStatistics`). Cross-tenant PII proof is **HUMAN_ONLY**.
  - **Mass Assignment:** `CinemaOperatingCompanyData.accessRightDashboard/FilmStatistics/BonusProgram/Campaigning` (caller-supplied) mirror `UserPrivileges` derived flags. `updateUser(adminCinemaOperatingCompanyIds:[ID!])` mirrors membership/role relationships.
  - **Dangling CNAME:** `web-dev.cineplex.de` CNAMEs to `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io` which returns NXDOMAIN (DoH Status 3, Azure SOA present), 17th+ consecutive cycle. Composes with the CORS suffix allowlist (claimability is provider-side).
  - **Staging Oracle:** `graphql-api.app.staging.cineplex.de` has `testing_getConfirmationCode` resolving unauthenticated (200, backend hit, 405-mismatch) vs prod `FORBIDDEN`. Field also exists on prod. Extraction is **HUMAN_ONLY**.
- **Dead/Rejected (Current State):** `api.cineplex.de` GET-based GraphQL bypass (strict 403 across methods), all TLS-dead hosts (`app.staging.cineplex.de`, `graphql-api.app.couat.cineplex.de`, `login.cineplex.de`, `sso.cineplex.de`), relay metrics/broker saturation at `data-9fc27eb430.cineplex.de` (descriptive-only), and all explicit program out-of-scope classes. `getOnlineTicketingBooking` SSRF lead was killed by a root-gated `FORBIDDEN` canary.

## Work State
### Completed
- **Knowledge Base Correction:** Canonical status added (`## CANONICAL STATUS (2026-09-30)`) to `knowledge/index.md`, partitioned into LIVE/DEAD/SURVIVING/METHOD RULES and stamping retracted claims. 
- **Publisher Integrity:** `scripts/sync-issues.py` parser behavior audited (only `[HYP]` blocks published). Residual falsified `IDOR` blocks cleared from the publish path (class `IDOR` went 297→0), decoder oracle retained as `class: ACCESS_CONTROL`. 
- **Harness Fixed:** `.github/workflows/hunt.yml` and `scripts/passive_verify.py` repaired (8 verifier defects fixed, brace truncation corrected), with `scripts/test_passive_verify.py` (14 offline tests) all passing. Offline replay over the real corpus now extracts filtered, balanced URLs only.
- **Full Schema Enumeration:** Read 385 types, 44 INPUT_OBJECT bodies, and all argument types for Query/Mutation on `graphql-api.app.cineplex.de` via unauthenticated balanced GETs (manual verification). 
- **CORS & Entry Points Verified:** Confirmed preflight + actual responses (6/6), DNS label boundary enforcement, `Origin:null` reflection, and arbitrary-path catch-all on both environments. GET-only mirrors (`/graphql`, `/api/graphql`, `/gql`) vs POST-capable root (`/`) mapped (4 paths × 2 envs).
- **Structural IDOR Verified:** 4/4 resolvers + 6/6 control gates confirmed via read-only GETs on public-id forms (no customer records touched). 

### Active
- **CORS Chain Assessment:** Evaluating the composition between dangling `web-dev.cineplex.de` and the CORS suffix allowlist with `ACAC:true` (precondition passive, claimability provider-side). 
- **Mass-Assignment & Auth Flags:** Documenting concrete, read-only evidence for `updateUser`, `login(privileged)`, `refreshLogin(privileged)`, `loginPOS(authToken)`, `startWebBooking`, `logUserScreeningInterests`, `sendNotifications`, `deleteCineplexUser`, `increaseUserTestingStatus`, and `storeSDKLogin`/`storeConsent`. These require AUTH_HELPED verification and must not be executed against live data.
- **Staging Oracle:** Tracking environment-guard omission for `testing_getConfirmationCode` across 10+ cycles; extraction remains HUMAN_ONLY.

### Blocked
- **Automated Verification:** `probe-results.md` cannot be trusted to accept/reject hypotheses. All automated inferences that rely on its 403/400s are void until a fixed verifier runs and produces replayable evidence. 
- **Provider Attestation:** Claimability of `web.gentleglacier-dfef6458.switzerlandnorth.azurecontainerapps.io` (Azure Container Apps) for `web-dev.cineplex.de` takeover is outstanding and required to move the chain from precondition to complete finding.
- **Cross-Tenant IDOR Proof & Staging POST Oracle:** Both require human interaction with accounts/customer data (consented, out-of-band) per program constraints, blocking passive-only submission despite strong structural evidence.
- **Remediation Scope:** GraphQL schema exposure is path-pattern-based (arbitrary unshadowed paths), not fixed to named routes; CORS remediation must account for the label-boundary logic and the `null`/cross-env origins.

## Next Move
1. **Immediate:** Execute the fixed verifier against a small, balanced URL set for `graphql-api.app.{cineplex.de,staging.cineplex.de}` (root `/`, `/graphql`, one arbitrary path, and `?query={__typename}`), capture request lines + status + headers, and diff against `probe-results.md` artifacts to confirm the 8 defects are eliminated. Save results to a new, replayable log (do not overwrite `probe-results.md` blindly).
2. **Next:** With verified balanced probes, confirm `OPTIONS /` actual-response CORS headers for the 4 Origins (`null`, `http://localhost:3000`, `https://app.staging.cineplex.de`, and a negative control `evilcineplex.de`) on prod+staging via manual curl (read-only), then document the exact `ACAO/ACAC/ACAM/ACAH` values in evidence. Do not test mutations.

## Relevant Files
- `knowledge/index.md`: Canonical status, program constraints, rejection rationale, and the living correction history (must be read first for retrieval context, not just appended to).
- `scripts/passive_verify.py`: Replaced extractor module (testable, 14 offline tests). Use for URL extraction over corpus (balanced, filtered).
- `scripts/test_passive_verify.py`: Offline test suite to validate extractor behavior before running against real targets.
- `scripts/sync-issues.py`: Publisher logic (parse_blocks matches `^\[HYP\]` only; uses fingerprints and near-duplicate collapse). Understand its behavior before any tracker writes.
- `.github/workflows/hunt.yml`: Hunt workflow containing the 8 fixed verifier defects (reference for scope of fixes).
- `inventory/cineplex.md`: Full inventory of 132 hosts; `scope.yml`: Program scope (verify any new host against scope before testing).
- `leads/lead-bigpickle.md` and `leads/lead-nemotron3.md`: Active lead files containing `[HYP]` blocks (read for current survivors, but never trust as canonical without cross-checking against `knowledge/index.md`).
- `reports/analyst-nemotron3.log`: Analyst log; treat as untrusted peer output (not to be adopted as evidence).
- `probe-results.md`: Legacy probe log (harness-defective). Do not infer negatives from it; only use for timestamp correlation after the fixed verifier is run.
